# A raw NUL byte in a source file makes git classify it as binary, and every diff of it renders as
# "Binary files differ" — including on GitHub, which reads this file. scripts/ingest.ts carried one
# for its whole history, so the script that writes to the chunks table was never reviewable in a
# pull request. The byte is gone, but the attribute keeps a future one from silently doing it again.
*.ts diff
*.tsx diff
